«
    @ σConcord: are two measurements X = a±σb and Y = c±σd compatible? The
    @ question is about their difference D = Y − X, normal with mean d = c − a and
    @ standard deviation σD = √(σX² + σY² − 2ρ·σX·σY), ρ being the global variable
    @ ρ that the arithmetic of the core also uses (0 if it does not exist).
    @ Draws the law of D, marks zero, shades the two tails that make the p-value,
    @ and returns, tagged: d, σD, z = |d|/σD and p = 2·UTPN(0,1,z). No verdict:
    @ the threshold belongs to the user. Y is expressed in the unit of X; a plain
    @ number counts as exact. Bounds a…b, a±b, a±p% are refused: see ΔConcord.
    @ Two ±σ bars that do not touch can still be compatible: 10±σ1 and 12.2±σ1
    @ give p = 0.12.

    @ Value and standard deviation of a value without unit: V → a σ
    «
        DUP TypeName → ScK
        «
            CASE
                ScK "uncertain" == THEN Object→ END
                ScK "range" == ScK "drange" == OR ScK "prange" == OR THEN
                    DROP "σConcord: bounds are not ±σ, use ΔConcord" DoError
                END
                ScK "integer" == ScK "neg_integer" == OR ScK "decimal" == OR
                ScK "neg_decimal" == OR ScK "fraction" == OR ScK "neg_fraction" == OR
                ScK "bignum" == OR ScK "neg_bignum" == OR THEN 0 END
                DROP "σConcord: X and Y must be a±σb values or numbers" DoError
            END
        »
    »
    @ Pixel column of a value: V Min Max Left Right → #x
    «
        → ScV ScMin ScMax ScL ScR
        « ScV ScMin - ScMax ScMin - ÷ ScR ScL - × ScL + 0 RND R→B »
    »
    → ScSplit ScPix
    «
        → ScX ScY
        «
            @ Refuse bounds before anything is put on the stack
            ScX ScY 2 →List 1 2
            FOR ScJ
                DUP ScJ GET IF DUP TypeName "unit" == THEN UVAL END TypeName
                IF DUP "range" == OVER "drange" == OR SWAP "prange" == OR THEN
                    DROP "σConcord: bounds are not ±σ, use ΔConcord" DoError
                END
            NEXT
            DROP
            @ Y in the unit of X; the unit kept aside as 1_unit (or 1)
            IF ScX TypeName "unit" == THEN
                IF ScY TypeName "unit" ≠ THEN "σConcord: X has a unit, Y has none" DoError END
                ScY ScX Convert 'ScY' STO
                1 ScX →Unit ScX UVAL ScY UVAL
            ELSE
                IF ScY TypeName "unit" == THEN "σConcord: Y has a unit, X has none" DoError END
                1 ScX ScY
            END
            SWAP ScSplit ROT ScSplit
            IFERR 'ρ' RCL THEN DROP 0 END
            → ScU ScA ScSA ScC ScSC ScRho
            «
                ScC ScA -
                ScSA SQ ScSC SQ + 2 ScRho × ScSA × ScSC × -
                IF DUP 0 ≤ THEN DROP "σConcord: no uncertainty left on D = Y − X" DoError END
                √
                → ScD ScS
                «
                    ScD ABS ScS ÷
                    DUP 0 1 ROT UTPN 2 ×
                    ScD 4 ScS × - 0 MIN ScD 4 ScS × + 0 MAX
                    FromLCD Size DROP B→R
                    → ScZ ScP ScMin ScMax ScW
                    «
                        ClearLCD
                        "σConcord: law of D = Y − X" { #0d #2d 1 true false } DrawText
                        @ Axis at row 150, peak at row 34; curve drawn as 160 segments;
                        @ where |D − d| ≥ |d|, a vertical stroke shades the tail
                        24 ScW 12 - 150 34
                        → ScL ScR ScBase ScTop
                        «
                            ScMin ScMin ScMax ScL ScR ScPix ScBase R→B 2 →List
                            ScMax ScMin ScMax ScL ScR ScPix ScBase R→B 2 →List DrawLine
                            ScMin ScMin ScMax ScL ScR ScPix ScBase R→B 2 →List
                            → ScPrev
                            «
                                0 160
                                FOR ScJ
                                    ScMin ScMax ScMin - ScJ × 160 ÷ +
                                    → ScT
                                    «
                                        ScT ScMin ScMax ScL ScR ScPix
                                        ScBase ScBase ScTop - ScT ScD - ScS ÷ SQ -2 ÷ EXP × - 0 RND R→B
                                        2 →List
                                        DUP ScPrev SWAP DrawLine
                                        IF ScT ScD - ABS ScD ABS ≥ THEN
                                            DUP 1 GET ScBase R→B 2 →List DrawLine
                                        ELSE
                                            DROP
                                        END
                                        ScT ScMin ScMax ScL ScR ScPix
                                        ScBase ScBase ScTop - ScT ScD - ScS ÷ SQ -2 ÷ EXP × - 0 RND R→B
                                        2 →List 'ScPrev' STO
                                    »
                                NEXT
                            »
                            @ Zero, dashed from the top to the axis
                            0 ScMin ScMax ScL ScR ScPix
                            → ScZx
                            «
                                ScTop ScBase
                                FOR ScJ
                                    ScZx ScJ R→B 2 →List ScZx ScJ 4 + R→B 2 →List DrawLine
                                8 STEP
                                "0" ScZx B→R 3 - R→B #152d 2 →List 0 true false 3 →List + DrawText
                            »
                            @ The mark d, unless it would sit on top of the 0
                            ScD ScMin ScMax ScL ScR ScPix B→R 0 ScMin ScMax ScL ScR ScPix B→R
                            - ABS 12 ≥ IF THEN
                                "d" ScD ScMin ScMax ScL ScR ScPix B→R 3 - R→B #152d 2 →List
                                0 true false 3 →List + DrawText
                            END
                        »
                        @ X and Y, written over the upper left of the drawing
                        "X = " ScX →Str + { #0d #24d 0 true false } DrawText
                        "Y = " ScY →Str + { #0d #42d 0 true false } DrawText
                        @ The numbers
                        "d = " ScD -4 RND ScU × →Str + "     σD = " + ScS -4 RND ScU × →Str +
                        { #0d #172d 0 true false } DrawText
                        "z = |d| / σD = " ScZ -4 RND →Str + { #0d #192d 0 true false } DrawText
                        "p = 2·UTPN(0,1,z) = " ScP -4 RND →Str + "   (shaded)" +
                        { #0d #212d 0 true false } DrawText
                        ScD ScU × "d" →Tag ScS ScU × "σD" →Tag ScZ "z" →Tag ScP "p" →Tag
                    »
                »
            »
        »
    »
»
